ADDITIONAL GRANT — GAME MODS

The "NoDerivatives" restriction above applies to the source code and the
game itself (the "Original Work"). However, this license explicitly
permits the creation and distribution of "Mods" — supplementary files,
data, scripts, or packages that are loaded by the game at runtime through
the official modding system, and that do not modify or replace the
Original Work's source code or binaries.

Mods are considered independent works and are NOT derivative works of the
Original Work, provided that:

  1. The Mod is distributed as a separate, standalone package and does not
     include or embed the Original Work's source code or binaries.
  2. The Mod is loaded at runtime via the official modding API provided by
     the game.
  3. The Mod does not circumvent or remove any technical protection,
     licensing, or attribution mechanisms of the Original Work.

Authors of Mods retain full rights to their own work and may choose any
license for their Mods.

